9.	Python Programs to create bar graph

Source Code:

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Data
courses = ['Python', 'Java', 'C++', 'JavaScript', 'SQL']
students_enrolled = [120, 85, 60, 95, 110]

# Create Bar Graph
plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))
plt.bar(courses, students_enrolled, color='teal', edgecolor='black', width=0.6)
plt.title('Course Enrollment Numbers')
plt.xlabel('Courses')
plt.ylabel('Number of Students Enrolled')
plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)
plt.show()



10.	Python Programs to create Line graph

Source Code:

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Data
months = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun']
sales = [12000, 15000, 14000, 18000, 22000, 25000]

# Create Line Graph
plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))
plt.plot(months, sales, marker='o', color='crimson', linestyle='-', linewidth=2, markersize=8)
plt.title('Monthly Sales Performance')
plt.xlabel('Month')
plt.ylabel('Sales (in ₹)')
plt.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.6)
plt.show()


